    "explanation": "To both parties: the disputed charge of SGD 37.74 stands. No refund and no compensation is due, because the longer route is fully excused by a road closure that the record documents.\n\nDistance. On the platform's own figures the booked optimal route (BKE southbound then PIE westbound) is 24.0 km, and the GPS trace measured 29.98 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff — an excess of 5.98 km, or 24.9% of optimal. The trace figure governs; the rounded 30.0 km on the trip record may not be cited for the threshold test (POL-RD-01). That passes both limbs of the POL-RD-01 gate, so a deviation is established on this trip's own evidence, and the rider is right that the trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip_id TRP-00111 and the same 07:47:40 pickup event, shifting the burden to the driver (POL-RD-08).\n\nWhy no refund follows. The excess is exonerated under POL-RD-03. EV-ADVIS-00111-01 is a real, on-file LTA record at weight 1.0 — a HIGH-severity vehicle fire closing all lanes of the PIE towards Tuas between Clementi Rd and Jalan Anak Bukit, active 07:10–09:30, overlapping the trip window by 41.5 minutes. That is an expressway segment the booked optimal route traverses (intersects_route = true), so the naming condition is met; the validity window covers the time the vehicle would have reached the segment, including the 15-minute buffer; and the platform's own trace assessment records the vehicle leaving the optimal corridor at Bukit Panjang, before the closed segment, and rejoining the route to the destination afterwards on the AYE. The rider's argument that the AYE is not the optimal corridor and so the rejoin condition fails is considered and rejected: the condition is that the actual route leave the corridor before the affected segment and rejoin the route to the destination after it, which the record shows, and reading it to demand re-entry onto the identical carriageway would defeat the clause in exactly the situation it names. The diversion is also minimal: the shortest lawful alternative is 29.2 km against the 24.0 km optimal, and the driver drove 29.98 km — only 0.78 km more, inside the 1.0 km tolerance. The exoneration cap is 1.30 × (29.2 − 24.0) + 1.0 = 7.76 km, and the whole 5.98 km excess falls under it, so the closure-adjusted optimal is 24.0 + 5.98 = 29.98 km with a duration of 37.5 minutes (the booked 30.0 minutes scaled to the adjusted distance).\n\nThe money. Against the closure-adjusted optimal the recomputed fare is (3.80 + 0.75 × 29.98 + 0.28 × 37.5) × 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, + 0.80 platform fee = 37.585. Charged_total 37.74 less 37.585 leaves a residual of 0.155, below the SGD 0.50 de minimis, which is why the outcome is NO_ACTION and the charge stands. The rider's figure of SGD 6.75 is the arithmetic that would apply only if no exoneration ran — a recomputed fare of 31.00 against the booked 24.0 km and a refund of 6.74 rounded up to 6.75 — but POL-RD-03 displaces it, and POL-RD-02 is expressly run against the adjusted optimal once POL-RD-03 excuses the excess.\n\nOther points. No rider-requested detour runs (POL-RD-04): the only chat exchange is the driver's own notice at 07:54:20 and the rider's reply 'as long as i reach by 8.30'; neither identifies a place or road for the driver to act on and the message's waypoint_hint is null, so the clause is unavailable — as the rider correctly says. The rider's assertion that he saw no closure cites no artifact and carries no weight against the on-file advisory (POL-RD-08); the driver's in-app notice and the rider's non-objection are noted but the outcome does not rest on them. No ERP correction is due: tolls_erp is 0.00 and erp_gantries is empty, so there is nothing to refund under POL-RD-09(2) and no unmatched charge line to refer. No full-refund uplift runs (POL-RD-06): the deviation is not MATERIAL (5.98 km is below 8.0 km, 24.9% below 50%) and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 588 completed_trips_90d, so no repeat pattern is established and no conduct referral is produced. The profile fields touched in the debate (the driver's lifetime prior_deviation_flags, the rider's claim history) are context only under POL-GEN-01 and were not used to establish anything about this trip. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: the identifiers match, the trace is unbroken (229 fixes, 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps), the advisory is present and covers the window, and no charge line lacks a counterpart."
